        <p>A restless night. Time alone. A loud truck. A tense walk. Each experience can leave a little stress behind before your dog has fully settled from the last one.</p>
        <p class="cp-mechanism-name">There is a name for this: <strong>trigger stacking.</strong></p>
        <p>Think of it like a bucket slowly filling with water. Each stressful moment adds a little more. As the water rises, the amount of room left in the bucket gets smaller.</p>
        <p>That remaining room is your dog's <strong>Safety Margin.</strong></p>
        <p>Eventually, the doorbell, a passing dog, or an unexpected touch becomes <span class="cp-highlight"><strong>the final drop that makes the bucket overflow.</strong></span></p>
